  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Ford Fiesta?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. Fuel level is the powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel signal, which you can query through the GraphQL Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. The segments resource can also detect refuel events and return the level signal at the start and end of each one."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Ford Fiesta with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API. Then query vehicle data from the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Ford Fiesta?",
      "a": "The DIMO LTE R1 entry lists the dtc event and the obdDTCList, obdStatusDTCCount and obdDistanceWithMIL signals. The Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks) posts to your targetURL when a condition you configure is met."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Ford Fiesta?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device and the segments query in the Telemetry API with the idling detection mechanism, which requires a DIMO device. It treats periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range as segments. You can tune the threshold with maxIdleRpm, which defaults to 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Ford Fiesta mileage?",
      "a": "A DIMO device reports the odometer signal, powertrainTransmissionTravelledDistance, in km. To get verifiable proof of the reading, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint, then retrieve the resulting credential through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a Ford Fiesta vehicle data API through a DIMO device, the connection type listed for this model, covering 2012 and newer model years. This coverage is tested, not just expected. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance."
